.SH "نام (NAME)"
mysql2dlf \- convert mysql logfiles to dlf format
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBmysql2dlf\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBmysql2dlf\fR converts a MySQL query log file to DLF format.  Information on
MySQL can be found on http://www.mysql.org/. The query log file is defined
by the \-\-log[=file] option of \fBmysqld\fR, or the log=file setting in MySQL
configuration file.
.PP
Such a log file looks like e.g.
.PP
.Vb 9
\& /usr/sbin/mysqld, Version: 3.23.43\-debug\-log, started with:
\& Tcp port: 3306  Unix socket: /var/run/mysqld/mysqld.sock
\& Time                 Id Command    Argument
\& 011218 15:02:58       1 Connect     root@localhost on
\&                       1 Query       SHOW VARIABLES LIKE \*(Aqpid_file\*(Aq
\&                       1 Shutdown
\& 011226 21:35:59       6 Connect     joe@localhost on
\&                       6 Init DB     nmrshiftdb
\&                       6 Query       SHOW VARIABLES
.Ve
.PP
or
.PP
.Vb 11
\&                  42401 Query       SELECT
\&                  bannerID,
\&                  banner,
\&                  format,
\&                  width,
\&                  height,
\&                  alt,
\&                  url
\&              FROM
\&                  banners
\&              WHERE
\&
\&                  act = \*(Aqtrue\*(Aq  AND (keyw = \*(Aqfullsize\*(Aq OR keyw = \*(Aqglobal\*(Aq)
.Ve
.PP
The generic database dlf format is described in database.xml.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
To process a log as produced by MySQL:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $ mysql2dlf < mysql\-log
.Ve
.PP
mysql2dlf will be rarely used on its own, but is more likely
called by lr_log2report:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $ lr_log2report mysql < /var/log/mysql\-log
.Ve
.SH "نکات (NOTES)"
.IX Header "NOTES"
The parser has been tested for query log files for MySQL 3.23.46 only.
.SH "اشکالات (BUGS)"
.IX Header "BUGS"
This converter stores all log files information in one big nested array in
memory, before writing.  Therefore, memory consumption is linear with the
size of the log.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBmysql\fR\|(1), \fBmysqld\fR\|(1)
